/blackmail
Blackmail fail
Gwern
2013-12-10
2020-11-12

bitcoin cs/cryptography personal
<div class="page-description-annotation">
<p>In which the author receives surprising offers from kind strangers</p>
</div>
<p>In September <span class="date-range">2012<sub><span title="2012 was 14 years ago.">14ya</span></sub></span>, I was extorted for <span class="inflation-adjusted" data-year-original="2012" data-amount-original="32" data-year-current="2026" data-amount-current="48.76" title="CPI inflation-adjusted US dollar: from nominal $32 in 2012 → real $48.76 in 2026">$48.76<span class="subsup"><sup>$32</sup><sub>2012</sub></span></span> for being gwern; I declined to pay. In November <span class="date-range">2013<sub><span title="2013 was 13 years ago.">13ya</span></sub></span>, I called an encryption bluff that I was Dread Pirate Roberts. In December <span class="date-range">2013<sub><span title="2013 was 13 years ago.">13ya</span></sub></span>, a crazy person tried to blackmail me for billions of dollars for being <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satoshi_Nakamoto">Satoshi Nakamoto</a>; I declined to pay. In March <span class="date-range">2014<sub><span title="2014 was 12 years ago.">12ya</span></sub></span>, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darknet_market" id="_5BgTlCyj" class="link-annotated-partial link-live" data-link-icon="wikipedia" data-link-icon-type="svg" data-url-iframe="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darknet_market#bodyContent" title="Darknet market">DNM</a> Evolution threatened to dox me if I did not reveal information about their security vulnerabilities. In February <span class="date-range">2015<sub><span title="2015 was 11 years ago.">11ya</span></sub></span>, an Agora user doxed me in an unexpected way and I paid a small bounty.</p>
